The {{nihongo|'''Kawaei clan'''|川栄氏|Kawaei-shi}} was a [[Sanese clan|Sanese samurai clan]]. Kawaei clan was the branch of Soga Clan prior to the split of Nakamizu from Miyagi Empire. Kawaei clan was a minor clan in [[Nakamizu|Southern Court]], ruled Southern part of Kinugasa Province. Kawaei clan was known as the unifier of Nakamizu under the lead of Sannedaina ([[Kawaei Rena]], [[Kawaei Yoshiyuki]] and [[Kawaei Yoshifumi]]). Until the first imperial restoration in 1801, Kawaei clan was the leader of Southern Court (outside imperial leader). After the democratization of Nakamizu, Kawaei Clan no longer in its political position, though some of the descendant of Kawaei currently active in Nakamizu government.

==History==
===Prior to 1598===
===Rise to power===
===="Sannedaina"====
As the passing of [[Kawaei Shigetaka]], his 4 children [[Kawaei Rena|Rena]], [[Kawaei Yoshiyuki|Yoshiyuki]], [[Kawaei Yoshifumi|Yoshifumi]] and [[Kawaei Kaiyo|Kaiyo]] left with the will of Rena as the proper successor of his rule. However, Rena implicitly declined by deciding that all of her younger siblings to inherit the sovereign of the clan with her as the decision maker. Later on, the youngest Kaiyo decided to let her older siblings to held the clan leadership while she just taking order from them. The 3 siblings later referred as "Sannedaina" (三姉弟名) which meaning the sovereign of 3 siblings with emphasis of older sister and younger brothers on the kanji characters. These clan heads will lead the movement to unify the fragmented Southern Court with declining Kanemoto Shogunate influences.
====Kawaei Yoshiyuki unification====
====Invasion of Kaesong and Ming====
After completely unified southern court area, in 1620, Kawaei Yoshiyuki aiming to rule over [[Zong]] with using [[Shansi]] as the stepping stone toward the Jade Peninsula. Although having much negative reactions from his vassals, Yoshiyuki start to launch his campaign to southeast Shansi via the western tip of Suzuya island by sending 80,000 soldiers under various clans into the mainland. 

